# nanopb generator options for APPInfomationData.proto
# (the V0 pairing handshake: 0xA201/0xA301 APP_INFO_DATA, SN-keyed AES-128-CBC)
#
# The HiFlow Pro emits its 16-byte encRand (= the V1/AES-GCM session key) inside
# the pairing reply: the outer message's field 8 carries the APPDtuInfoMO, whose
# field 27 is enc_rand (walked exactly like this in the reference implementation,
# test/ref/hiflow_ble/hiflow.py::_extract_enc_rand_from_appinfo).
#
# Only two fields need static storage; everything else stays a pb_callback_t,
# which nanopb skips while decoding when no callback is registered (see
# pb_decode.c: decode_callback_field -> pb_skip_field). That keeps the reply
# decode allocation-free and immune to a device that reports more meters / PV
# strings / features than we would have guessed with max_count.
#
#   * APPDtuInfoMO.enc_rand          : the value we are after, exactly 16 bytes.
#   * APPInfoDataResDTO.time_ymd_hms : we *send* that message (like the
#                                      reference lib), so it must be encodable
#                                      without a callback.
#
# NOTE: deliberately max_size, not fixed_length. With (nanopb).fixed_length an
# empty bytes field decodes to 16 zero bytes, which would be accepted as a fresh
# encRand and then fail every GCM auth tag; with max_size the `.size` member
# lets hiflow_appinfo_extract_enc_rand() reject anything that is not exactly 16
# bytes, matching the reference implementation's explicit length check.
APPDtuInfoMO.enc_rand          max_size:16
APPInfoDataResDTO.time_ymd_hms max_size:24
